<p>When <span class="Term-Soft">Auto Tray Select</span> is selected, a paper 
 tray containing paper of the appropriate size and type will be selected 
 automatically. However, if several paper trays are loaded with paper of 
 the same size, your document might not be printed on the paper you intend. 
 To make sure that the correct paper is selected, you can specify the tray 
 containing paper to print onto before printing.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Paper</span> menu 
 on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> 
 list, select the paper tray containing the paper you want to print onto.</p></li>
<li><p>If <span class="Term-Soft">Bypass Tray</span> is 
 selected, click the <span class="Term-Soft">Position in bypass tray...</span> 
 button to open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the direction of paper loaded in the bypass 
 tray.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
